// The customer portal (W2b schema wave 21/22, B-W2b-157; plan W2b-3; design 02 portal-links: portal.customer.neworder,
// portal.customer.orders, links.pay; features SAL-072, SAL-073, SAL-074, SAL-077, SAL-078, FIN-118, FIN-123): what a
// customer sends from the portal or a link. An order request (picked styles, a past order copied, a sheet uploaded) is NOT
// an order: the office makes the order or a quote from it (prices again) or refuses it in words, so the sales-order state
// machine of sales.prisma does not change (SalesOrder has no DRAFT, plan §9). A change or cancel request asks for a
// change of a confirmed order; the office accepts it with W2a's amendment command (SalesOrderAmendment) or refuses it in
// words; the cut-off rules it is checked against are SalesSettings' (sales.prisma). A payment intent is one card or SEPA
// payment of a deposit request or an invoice at the payment provider: the provider's own fields take the card, so no card
// data ever reaches our database (FIN-123, PSD2 by the provider); its Payment is recorded by the payments command when
// the provider's signed webhook says it succeeded. The measurements a rider sends by link are MeasurementProfile
// revisions (parties.prisma).
//
// Who writes what (ownership/portal-sales.json; the …_portal_sales_w2b_guards triggers, redefined by the later waves, hold it
// for every login): a portal session (factory_partner_runtime behind its party's wall) writes its own drafts (the request,
// its lines and their sizes) and sends or withdraws them, asks for a change or a cancel of its own orders and withdraws the
// ask, and reads its own payment intents. The office (factory_runtime; the system context of the worker and the webhook)
// starts and fills a customer's draft too (OD s.1: its lines, sizes and people; discards only a draft an office person
// started), numbers and sends a draft for the portal (the partner role has no numbering grant) or for the customer at its
// Confirm, names the style drafts it made for a draft, decides requests and change requests, and makes and moves payment
// intents. The floor reads none of it. No cost or margin column anywhere; the price a customer was shown is the price grain.
//
// Every child row carries its parent's partyId in its reference, so it can never belong to another party than its
// request; uniqueness made of ids only (one open change request per order) is the API's, as in sales.prisma.
//
// B-CP-005 (customer page plan, schema wave "customer page 1/1"; design customer-page 12 §1-§2, 11 §1.1): the order
// request is THE one draft order of the portal. A draft grows step by step: lines of three kinds (catalogue, described,
// made to measure), the people of a by-person line (PortalOrderRequestPerson: a size, a measurement sheet or "sending
// later"), the parts marked "sending later", who saved it last, and the customer's own price per line (brandUnitPrice,
// the price grain), all frozen at Send. A draft with no line yet (only logos, only a sheet) may be kept and shared (OD s.1:
// and sent).
//
// OD s.1 (order start plan, schema wave "order start 1/1"; design order-start-2026-11-25 13-backend §1; Owner's yes 1a + 2a;
// Owner's change of 2026-11-25 10:12, addendum R1-R3: "we should not keep any requirements at all"): the draft is ONE draft
// order of both doors, started like a mail (a subject, a message = the note, attachments = the draft files) from its first
// input. The customer and the office (orders.manage over the company and the customer) both fill it; the office may also
// send it for the customer and confirm it in one command. NOTHING is required to start or to Send (not even a line): what
// the order needs (a style, a colourway, pieces by size, a price) is asked at Confirm. The lines are ONE products table
// whose every cell is optional: the product (a catalogue style or the customer's words), its sizing (standard, made to
// measure, or not decided yet), colour, pieces, open choices (choices: names only, never a price or a person). All frozen
// at Send. The style drafts the office made for a draft (styleIds) are office only: hidden from the customer's portal
// people, added while DRAFT or SENT.
//
// owb-b1 (order workflow build, schema wave "order workflow 1/1"; LF plan.md § 4, PL-schema § 3, § 5A rows 2-4): the draft
// and the sent request carry the order's picture (copied into the order at Confirm); a line may be taken out softly and put
// back (removedAt); a sent request may be taken back to DRAFT, keeping its number (the …_order_workflow_guards redefinition
// of the request's guard, G1). PaymentNotice: the customer's "I paid" (the customer's buyer tells us it paid; the office
// records the payment itself with its own command, then marks the notice RECORDED, or DISMISSED).

/// An order request from the portal (SAL-072, SAL-073, SAL-074; design portal.customer.neworder): a draft kept with us
/// while the customer (or the office for it, OD s.1) builds it (the portal's "Draft saved 10:42"), then sent with a number of the company's
/// PORTAL_REQUEST series ("our request RQ-0087"). The office makes the order or a quote from it (ACCEPTED, naming it) or
/// refuses it in words (REFUSED); the customer may withdraw it before that (WITHDRAWN). DRAFT → SENT → ACCEPTED | REFUSED
/// | WITHDRAWN; the last three are final. A draft is deleted when the customer discards it (it has no number); nothing
/// else is ever deleted. Its lines and sizes change only while it is a DRAFT.
model PortalOrderRequest {
  id            String                   @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId      String                   @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The selling company it asks.
  companyId     String                   @db.Uuid
  /// The customer (the partner role's policy key).
  partyId       String                   @db.Uuid
  /// The number from the company's PORTAL_REQUEST series, given when it is sent (null while DRAFT); unique in the company,
  /// never changed.
  number        String?
  /// How the customer started it: styles picked from the catalogue, a past order copied at today's prices, a sheet
  /// uploaded. One draft may gather lines of every way (each line names a copied order line).
  source        PortalOrderRequestSource @default(PICKER)
  /// Their purchase order number (the API asks it when the account requires one).
  customerRef   String?
  /// OD s.1 (addendum R2): the draft's subject, as a mail's ("Custom motorcycle suit for our race team"): 1 to 200 trimmed
  /// characters, null = none. A draft column of both doors (the customer's and the office's), frozen at Send; the draft's
  /// title (else its first line's words).
  subject       String?
  /// The delivery address asked: one of the party's own addresses, a SHIP_TO one, not archived when chosen. Null: the
  /// party's default.
  shipToAddressId String?                @db.Uuid
  /// The delivery date they would like (we confirm the date).
  requestedDate DateTime?                @db.Date
  /// Their note to us (OD s.1: the draft's message, as a mail's body).
  note          String?
  /// ISO 4217: the currency of the prices shown on its lines.
  currency      String                   @default("EUR")
  status        PortalOrderRequestStatus @default(DRAFT)
  /// When it was sent, and who sent it (a person of the customer or of the office); set exactly from SENT on, never changed.
  sentAt        DateTime?                @db.Timestamptz(3)
  sentById      String?                  @db.Uuid
  /// The office's decision: when and by whom (set exactly when ACCEPTED or REFUSED), and the words of a refusal (exactly
  /// when REFUSED).
  decidedAt     DateTime?                @db.Timestamptz(3)
  decidedById   String?                  @db.Uuid
  refuseReason  String?
  /// What it became (ACCEPTED: exactly one, of the same company and party): the order the office made from it, or the
  /// quote it sent instead.
  salesOrderId  String?                  @db.Uuid
  quoteId       String?                  @db.Uuid
  /// Set exactly when WITHDRAWN.
  withdrawnAt   DateTime?                @db.Timestamptz(3)
  version       Int                      @default(1)
  createdAt     DateTime                 @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt     DateTime                 @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// Who started the draft: a person of the customer or of the office (OD s.1).
  createdById   String?                  @db.Uuid
  // ── B-CP-005 (customer page plan, schema wave "customer page 1/1"; S3): the one draft order grows step by step.
  /// The parts the customer marked "Sending later" (logos, references, people), each once; empty: none. Changed only while
  /// it is a DRAFT (with its other draft columns), frozen once sent.
  laterParts     PortalDraftPart[]       @default([])
  /// Who saved the draft last and when ("Saved 10:42 by …"): a person of the customer or of the office (OD s.1); both or
  /// neither; written with every save while it is a DRAFT, frozen once sent.
  lastEditedById String?                 @db.Uuid
  lastEditedAt   DateTime?               @db.Timestamptz(3)
  // ── end B-CP-005
  // ── OD s.1 (order start plan, schema wave "order start 1/1"; 13-backend §1a)
  /// The style drafts the office made for this draft ("Make style draft"), in the order they were made (styles of its
  /// company or tenant-wide, our own collection or its customer's private label; each once, at most 50); empty at insert,
  /// only added, while it is a DRAFT or SENT. Office only: hidden from its customer's portal people (the portal reads only
  /// whether the design started). od-fx1: the default is the DATABASE's only (dbgenerated, as fileIds and mentionedUserIds): with
  /// `@default([])` Prisma named the column in every INSERT, and the partner role holds no column grant on it (a portal draft and
  /// the seed's buyer inserts were refused, 42501).
  styleIds       String[]                @default(dbgenerated("('{}'::text)::uuid[]")) @db.Uuid
  // ── end OD s.1
  // ── owb-b1 (order workflow build, schema wave "order workflow 1/1"; PL-schema § 3, § 5A row 2)
  /// The order's picture, as on SalesOrder (the same three names): a file of the tenant, an image or a PDF, never a fiscal
  /// archive, body data or audio (the …_order_workflow_guards trigger, G2); null: the first line's design. Written by its
  /// customer's portal people or the office while it is a DRAFT or SENT (a draft column, and the one SENT → SENT change
  /// both doors may make: G1); frozen once decided. Confirm copies the three into the order it makes. All or none (G2).
  /// Readable by its customer, who sees who set it, like lastEditedById.
  pictureFileId  String?                 @db.Uuid
  pictureSetAt   DateTime?               @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// Who set the picture: a person of the customer or of the office.
  pictureSetById String?                 @db.Uuid
  // ── end owb-b1

  company    Company                  @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  party      Party                    @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId and partyId.
  shipTo     PartyAddress?            @relation("PortalOrderRequestShipTo", fields: [tenantId, partyId, shipToAddressId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  salesOrder SalesOrder?              @relation("PortalOrderRequestOrder", fields: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, salesOrderId], references: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  quote      Quote?                   @relation("PortalOrderRequestQuote", fields: [tenantId, partyId, quoteId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  lines      PortalOrderRequestLine[]
  // B-CP-005 (S2): the people named on its lines (a roster), removed with their line or the discarded draft.
  people     PortalOrderRequestPerson[]
  // owb-b1 (order workflow build, schema wave "order workflow 1/1"): its picture (Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default: that
  // would also clear tenantId); the customer's own columns used on its lines (order-columns.prisma), removed with the
  // discarded draft.
  picture        StoredFile?          @relation("PortalOrderRequestPicture", fields: [tenantId, pictureFileId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  lineColumnUses OrderLineColumnUse[] @relation("OrderLineColumnUseRequest")

  @@unique([tenantId, companyId, number])
  // The target of its lines' reference: a line of the same party.
  @@unique([tenantId, partyId, id])
  // The office's Approvals source (what waits) and the customer's drafts.
  @@index([tenantId, status])
  @@index([tenantId, partyId, status])
  // The request an order came from.
  @@index([tenantId, salesOrderId])
}

/// How an order request was started (design portal.customer.neworder "How do you want to order?").
enum PortalOrderRequestSource {
  /// Styles picked from the customer's catalogue (SAL-071).
  PICKER
  /// A past order copied at today's prices, every difference named (SAL-072).
  REORDER
  /// A sheet uploaded, with a dry run per row (SAL-073).
  UPLOAD
}

/// DRAFT (kept with us while the customer builds it) → SENT (numbered; it waits for the office) → ACCEPTED (the order or
/// quote made from it) | REFUSED (in words) | WITHDRAWN (by the customer, before the office decided).
enum PortalOrderRequestStatus {
  DRAFT
  SENT
  ACCEPTED
  REFUSED
  WITHDRAWN
}

/// One line of an order request: one style in one colourway, the size run in its size rows, the price the customer was
/// shown. Written by the customer or the office (OD s.1) while the request is a DRAFT; frozen when it is sent. OD s.1
/// (addendum R3): a row of the draft's products table, every cell optional — a CATALOGUE line names its style (its colourway
/// may wait), a DESCRIBED line may have no words yet, a MADE_TO_MEASURE line no garment type yet (still by person).
/// B-CP-005 (customer page plan, schema wave "customer page 1/1"; S1, M6): a line of one of three kinds — CATALOGUE (a
/// style in a colourway, as before), DESCRIBED (the customer's own words, colours in words, maybe its own style, a total or
/// sizes) or MADE_TO_MEASURE (a garment type, maybe a style, always by person) — its people in PortalOrderRequestPerson, and
/// the customer's own price beside the one it was shown. The …_customer_page_guards trigger holds each kind's shape.
model PortalOrderRequestLine {
  id                String   @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId          String   @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The request's party (the partner role's policy key).
  partyId           String   @db.Uuid
  requestId         String   @db.Uuid
  /// The line's place on the request: 1, 2, 3 …
  seq               Int
  /// B-CP-005: a CATALOGUE line names its style (OD s.1, addendum R3: its colourway may wait, "Colour: not picked yet"); a
  /// DESCRIBED or MADE_TO_MEASURE line may name the customer's own style, or neither. A colourway only with its style.
  styleId           String?  @db.Uuid
  colourwayId       String?  @db.Uuid
  /// A reorder's line: the past order's line it was copied from (of the same party), so the draft names every
  /// difference again (price, style revision, size run, a style no longer sold) when it is opened later.
  sourceOrderLineId String?  @db.Uuid
  /// The net unit price the customer was shown (their price list's, on that day), frozen when the request is sent; at
  /// least 0. Null: no price was shown (a portal role without prices). The office prices again when it makes the order.
  /// @grain price
  unitPriceShown    Decimal? @db.Decimal(18, 6)
  /// Their note on the line (their own style code, a remark).
  note              String?
  version           Int      @default(1)
  createdAt         DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt         DateTime @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdById       String?  @db.Uuid
  // ── B-CP-005 (S1, M6)
  /// What kind of line it is (CATALOGUE by default, as every line before this wave).
  kind              PortalDraftLineKind @default(CATALOGUE)
  /// What the customer wants, in its own words (1 to 2000 characters). OD s.1 (addendum R3): optional on every kind, a
  /// DESCRIBED line too (a row may be saved before its words).
  description       String?
  /// The colours in the customer's words (up to 200), for a line with no colourway of ours.
  colourText        String?
  /// MADE_TO_MEASURE: the garment type, a MeasurementTemplate code (that it is an ACTIVE one is the API's). OD s.1 (addendum
  /// R3): optional, asked at Confirm when the quote needs it.
  garmentType       String?
  /// DESCRIBED: the pieces in all, when the customer gives a total instead of sizes (1 to 100 000).
  quantity          Int?
  /// Its pieces are its people (PortalOrderRequestPerson): always on a MADE_TO_MEASURE line.
  byPerson          Boolean  @default(false)
  /// The customer's own net unit price for the line, typed in the draft by a portal role that sees prices; at least 0;
  /// frozen at Send with the rest of the line. Null: not typed. Carried into the order's OrderBrandPrice on accept.
  /// @grain price
  brandUnitPrice    Decimal? @db.Decimal(18, 6)
  // ── end B-CP-005
  // ── OD s.1 (order start plan, schema wave "order start 1/1"; 13-backend §1a; addendum R3)
  /// How the product is sized: STANDARD (sizes of a range, a total or people with sizes) or MADE_TO_MEASURE (exactly when the
  /// line's kind is MADE_TO_MEASURE: the line guard holds both together); null = "Not decided yet". The existing lines took
  /// it from their kind and pieces once (the back-fill in …_order_start_guards).
  sizing            PortalDraftSizing?
  /// The line's open choices ("Leather: Cowhide · Kangaroo · Not decided yet"): null = none; else 1 to 10 entries
  /// {topic, options, picked}: a topic of 1 to 60 trimmed characters, 2 to 6 distinct options of 1 to 60 trimmed
  /// characters, picked = one of the options or null ("Not decided yet"). Names only: never a price or a person. Written
  /// by the customer and the office while the request is a DRAFT (the line guard), frozen at Send.
  choices           Json?    @db.JsonB
  // ── end OD s.1
  // ── owb-b1 (order workflow build, schema wave "order workflow 1/1"; PL-schema § 5A row 3)
  /// Taken out of the draft ("Take it out", soft): when and by whom (a person of the customer or of the office), both
  /// together (the API); "Put it back" clears both. A line taken out still holds its cells and sizes, is not counted or sent, and
  /// goes with a discarded draft. Written while the request is a DRAFT, like every line cell (the line guard, unchanged).
  removedAt         DateTime? @db.Timestamptz(3)
  removedById       String?   @db.Uuid
  // ── end owb-b1

  request         PortalOrderRequest       @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId, requestId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // B-CP-005: optional (a DESCRIBED or MADE_TO_MEASURE line may name none); Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an
  // optional relation: that would also clear tenantId. A colourway without its style is refused by the guard (the
  // reference checks nothing while styleId is null).
  style           Style?                   @relation("PortalOrderRequestLineStyle", fields: [tenantId, styleId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  colourway       Colourway?               @relation("PortalOrderRequestLineColourway", fields: [tenantId, styleId, colourwayId], references: [tenantId, styleId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  sourceOrderLine SalesOrderLine?          @relation("PortalOrderRequestLineSource", fields: [tenantId, partyId, sourceOrderLineId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  sizes           PortalOrderRequestSize[]
  // B-CP-005 (S2): the people on a by-person line, removed with it.
  people          PortalOrderRequestPerson[]
  // owb-b1 (order workflow build, schema wave "order workflow 1/1"): order-columns.prisma, the customer's own column values
  // on it, removed with it.
  ownValues       OrderLineOwnValue[]      @relation("OrderLineOwnValueRequestLine")

  @@unique([tenantId, requestId, seq])
  // The target of its size rows' reference: a size of the same party.
  @@unique([tenantId, partyId, id])
}

// ── B-CP-005 (customer page plan, schema wave "customer page 1/1"; S1–S3; lead change: "Saved measurements" comes later, so
// a person is measured by SIZE, SHEET or LATER only)

/// OD s.1 (order start plan, addendum R3): how a draft line's product is sized (its "Sizing" cell; null = Not decided yet).
enum PortalDraftSizing {
  /// Standard sizes: a size run, a total, or people with a size of the range.
  STANDARD
  /// Custom size, made to measure (the line's kind is MADE_TO_MEASURE exactly then).
  MADE_TO_MEASURE
}

/// What kind of draft line it is (design 12 §2, part 1 "What you need").
enum PortalDraftLineKind {
  /// A style of the customer's catalogue in one of its colourways, its sizes in the size rows.
  CATALOGUE
  /// Described by the customer: its words, colours in words, maybe its own style; a total or sizes.
  DESCRIBED
  /// Made to measure: a garment type, maybe a style; always by person.
  MADE_TO_MEASURE
}

/// How one person of a by-person line is measured (design 12 §2, part 4 "People & sizes").
enum PortalDraftMeasureBy {
  /// A size of the range (PortalOrderRequestPerson.size).
  SIZE
  /// A measurement sheet the customer uploaded to the draft (a MEASUREMENTS file of this request or one of its lines).
  SHEET
  /// The customer sends it later.
  LATER
}

/// A part of the draft the customer will send later (design 12 §2, the checklist's "Sending later").
enum PortalDraftPart {
  LOGOS
  REFERENCES
  PEOPLE
}

/// One person on a by-person line of an order request (a rider, a team member; design 12 §2, part 4): a name, maybe a
/// number, and one way to be measured — a size, a measurement sheet the customer uploaded, or "sending later". Written by
/// the customer or the office (OD s.1) while the request is a DRAFT (the …_customer_page_guards trigger), frozen once sent; removed with its line
/// or the discarded draft (cascade). Personal data of the person named (GDPR art. 6(1)(b): what the order needs); the
/// office reads it, the floor never. Its party is its request's (the reference holds it).
model PortalOrderRequestPerson {
  id                String               @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId          String               @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The request's party (the partner role's policy key).
  partyId           String               @db.Uuid
  requestId         String               @db.Uuid
  /// The line of this request the person is on (a by-person line).
  lineId            String               @db.Uuid
  /// The person's place on the line: 1, 2, 3 … (rows never jump).
  seq               Int
  /// The name as the customer wrote it, 1 to 120 trimmed characters.
  name              String
  /// Their number (a race or shirt number), up to 10 trimmed characters.
  number            String?
  measureBy         PortalDraftMeasureBy
  /// SIZE: the size, 1 to 40 trimmed characters (whether the range has it is the API's); null otherwise.
  size              String?
  /// SHEET: the measurement sheet, a MEASUREMENTS file of this request or one of its lines; null otherwise.
  measurementFileId String?              @db.Uuid
  /// The customer's note on the person, up to 1000.
  note              String?
  version           Int                  @default(1)
  createdAt         DateTime             @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt         DateTime             @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// Who added the person: a person of the customer or of the office (OD s.1).
  createdById       String?              @db.Uuid

  request          PortalOrderRequest     @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId, requestId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Cascade, onUpdate: Restrict)
  line             PortalOrderRequestLine @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId, lineId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Cascade, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId. A file is never
  // deleted (its row stays DELETED).
  measurementFile  StoredFile?            @relation("PortalOrderRequestPersonSheet", fields: [tenantId, measurementFileId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([tenantId, lineId, seq])
  // A request's people (the draft page, the office's read of a draft).
  @@index([tenantId, requestId])
}
// ── end B-CP-005

/// The pieces of one size of an order request's line (the size grid as rows); above 0. Written while the request is a
/// DRAFT. Whether the style offers the size, and the minimum per size, are the API's (the portal shows them per cell).
model PortalOrderRequestSize {
  id          String   @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId    String   @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The line's party (the partner role's policy key).
  partyId     String   @db.Uuid
  lineId      String   @db.Uuid
  /// A size code of the style's range.
  size        String
  quantity    Int
  version     Int      @default(1)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt   DateTime @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdById String?  @db.Uuid

  line PortalOrderRequestLine @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId, lineId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([tenantId, lineId, size])
}

/// A customer's request to change or cancel a confirmed order (SAL-077, SAL-078; design portal.customer.orders "Ask for
/// a change", "Ask to cancel"): what they ask (the lines and sizes in its rows, a date, an address, their reason), checked
/// before the click against the company's cut-off rules (SalesSettings; the API refuses in words). The office answers:
/// ACCEPTED (a change through W2a's amendment command, named here; a cancel of the whole order by cancelling it) or
/// REFUSED (in words); the customer may withdraw it while OPEN. OPEN → ACCEPTED | REFUSED | WITHDRAWN; all three final.
/// Asked only of an order that is CONFIRMED, IN_PRODUCTION or READY. Never deleted.
/// B-PR-23 (production plan, schema wave 4/5): the production asks (RUSH, HOLD, RESUME, SPLIT_SHIPMENT, SAMPLE_ROUND) with
/// their own columns; a PARTLY_SHIPPED order may still ask CANCEL (of its unshipped lines), RUSH, HOLD and RESUME. The office
/// may also counter: OPEN → COUNTERED (a COUNTER_OFFER approval request the customer answers) → ACCEPTED (the customer said
/// yes to the counter) | REFUSED | WITHDRAWN. One OPEN or COUNTERED request per order and kind (the API's, serialised per
/// order). A bulk ask of one customer gives its requests one batch.
/// B-SA-005 (sales page plan, schema wave "sales page 1/1"; lead picks R3, R10, P21): a DESIGN request (their words, the
/// lines it is about, up to 10 of the order's files); the ask's own message in the order's conversation; the product change
/// requests an accepted DESIGN request raised (changes.prisma ChangeRequest.orderChangeRequestId); the work-order changes an
/// accepted request left to do (order-apply.prisma).
model OrderChangeRequest {
  id              String                   @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId        String                   @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The order's company and party (the reference's keys; the party is the partner role's policy key).
  companyId       String                   @db.Uuid
  partyId         String                   @db.Uuid
  orderId         String                   @db.Uuid
  kind            OrderChangeRequestKind
  /// A cancel's reason: a code of the CANCEL reason list (reasons.prisma ReasonCode, kept as text); required on a CANCEL,
  /// none on a CHANGE.
  reasonCode      String?
  /// Their words: a change's note, a cancel's note. B-SA-005: a DESIGN request's words, required there (1 to 4000).
  reason          String?
  /// A change: the delivery date they would like, and the address they ask the goods to go to (one of their own
  /// addresses); null: unchanged. B-PR-23: the date also on a RUSH ("Urgent – asked": the need-by date, optional) and on a
  /// SPLIT_SHIPMENT (the first part's date); the address a change only.
  requestedDate   DateTime?                @db.Date
  shipToAddressId String?                  @db.Uuid
  status          OrderChangeRequestStatus @default(OPEN)
  /// The office's answer: its words (required to refuse), when and by whom; set exactly when ACCEPTED or REFUSED.
  answer          String?
  answeredAt      DateTime?                @db.Timestamptz(3)
  answeredById    String?                  @db.Uuid
  /// ACCEPTED: the amendment of the order it made (sales.prisma SalesOrderAmendment, of the same order), when the
  /// order's lines or dates changed by one; set once, never changed.
  amendmentId     String?                  @db.Uuid
  /// Set exactly when WITHDRAWN.
  withdrawnAt     DateTime?                @db.Timestamptz(3)
  // B-PR-23 (production plan, schema wave 4/5; lead picks L18, L26, R-50, R-65; review fixes R-09, R-14, R-35).
  /// The office's counter-offer (COUNTERED, then kept after the answer): the COUNTER_OFFER approval request the customer
  /// answers (links-depth.prisma ApprovalRequest, about this request, of its customer: the reference), when and by whom (an
  /// office person), and what it offers: a date, a fee, words (at least one of the three). Written once, at OPEN → COUNTERED.
  counterApprovalId String?                @db.Uuid
  counteredAt       DateTime?              @db.Timestamptz(3)
  counteredById     String?                @db.Uuid
  counterDate       DateTime?              @db.Date
  /// The fee the counter-offer asks, in minor units of the order's currency, 0 or more: a priced counter is answered only by
  /// the customer's Buyer or Admin; others read "A price may apply" (the API drops the amount without the price grain).
  /// @grain price
  counterFee        Int?
  counterNote       String?
  /// What the customer was shown before Send (the frozen fields, priced yes or no, the earliest date: B-PR-24's impact),
  /// kept as it was shown; never an amount (it holds no number). Written with the request, never changed.
  impact            Json?
  /// SAMPLE_ROUND only (required there): the kind of round asked (PRE_PRODUCTION, SIZE_SET, TOP_OF_PRODUCTION or BRAND).
  sampleKind        SampleKind?
  /// SAMPLE_ROUND, once ACCEPTED: the round it made (of the asked kind, for the request's customer, made after it was
  /// asked: samples.prisma SampleRound); set once.
  sampleRoundId     String?                @db.Uuid
  /// A customer's bulk ask (lead pick L26): its requests, one per order, share one batch; a batch holds one customer's
  /// requests of one kind (the database refuses a batch that would span two customers or two kinds). Never changes.
  batchId           String?                @db.Uuid
  // B-SA-005 (sales page plan, schema wave "sales page 1/1"; lead picks R3, R10, P21).
  /// DESIGN only: the order's files the customer sends with its words (0 to 10, each once): AVAILABLE files of this order or
  /// of one of its lines, shared with its own customer (the API also checks the content wall; they are uploaded first through
  /// the portal thread route). Never copied onto a style. The default is the database's ('{}'), so a portal insert may leave
  /// the column out, as Message.mentionedUserIds. Written with the request, never changed.
  fileIds           String[]               @default(dbgenerated("('{}'::text)::uuid[]")) @db.Uuid
  /// The ask's own message in the order's conversation (P21, B-SA-048): the customer's INBOUND message shared with it, on the
  /// order's thread (threads.prisma Message, of the same customer: the reference). Set with the ask, or once while the
  /// request still waits (OPEN or COUNTERED); never changed (withdrawing and answering never touch it); one request per
  /// message.
  askMessageId      String?                @db.Uuid
  version         Int                      @default(1)
  createdAt       DateTime                 @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt       DateTime                 @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// The partner user who asked.
  createdById     String?                  @db.Uuid

  order     SalesOrder               @relation("OrderChangeRequestOrder", fields: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, orderId], references: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId, partyId and orderId.
  shipTo    PartyAddress?            @relation("OrderChangeRequestShipTo", fields: [tenantId, partyId, shipToAddressId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  amendment SalesOrderAmendment?     @relation("OrderChangeRequestAmendment", fields: [tenantId, orderId, amendmentId], references: [tenantId, orderId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  lines     OrderChangeRequestLine[]
  // B-PR-23: the counter-offer's approval request (of the same customer), who countered, the sample round an accepted
  // SAMPLE_ROUND made. Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default (that would also clear tenantId and partyId).
  counterApproval ApprovalRequest? @relation("OrderChangeRequestCounter", fields: [tenantId, partyId, counterApprovalId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  counteredBy     User?            @relation("OrderChangeRequestCounteredBy", fields: [tenantId, counteredById], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  sampleRound     SampleRound?     @relation("OrderChangeRequestSampleRound", fields: [tenantId, sampleRoundId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // B-SA-005: the ask's message, shared with the request's own party (the party is in the reference); Restrict, not Prisma's
  // SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId and partyId. The product change requests an
  // accepted DESIGN request raised, and the work-order changes an accepted request left to do (order-apply.prisma).
  askMessage            Message?          @relation("OrderChangeRequestAskMessage", fields: [tenantId, partyId, askMessageId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  productChangeRequests ChangeRequest[]   @relation("ChangeRequestOrderChangeRequest")
  workOrderChanges      WorkOrderChange[] @relation("WorkOrderChangeRequest")

  // The target of its rows' reference: a row of the same party.
  @@unique([tenantId, partyId, id])
  // An amendment answers one request.
  @@unique([tenantId, amendmentId])
  // B-PR-23: a counter-offer counters one request; a sample round answers one request.
  @@unique([tenantId, counterApprovalId])
  @@unique([tenantId, sampleRoundId])
  // B-SA-005: a message asks one request.
  @@unique([tenantId, askMessageId])
  // The order's requests, and the office's Approvals source (what waits).
  @@index([tenantId, orderId, status])
  @@index([tenantId, status])
  // B-PR-23: a batch's requests (the office answers a batch as one group).
  @@index([tenantId, batchId])
}

/// What a customer asks of an order (design portal.customer.orders).
enum OrderChangeRequestKind {
  /// Quantities and sizes, the date, the delivery address.
  CHANGE
  /// The whole order, or some of its lines.
  CANCEL
  // B-PR-12 (production plan, schema wave 2/5; lead picks L7, L18, R-50): the production asks. RUSH is open to a customer
  // exactly while its urgency switch is on (PortalSettings.productionUrgencyOn); the other four while its limits list them
  // (PortalSettings.productionAskKinds). Their own columns and rules come with B-PR-23.
  /// "Urgent – asked": the order sooner than the quota or the stage lets the customer mark it (an optional need-by date).
  RUSH
  /// Pause the order's production.
  HOLD
  /// Go on with a paused order.
  RESUME
  /// Ship the order in more than one delivery.
  SPLIT_SHIPMENT
  /// One more sample round before production.
  SAMPLE_ROUND
  // B-SA-005 (sales page plan, schema wave "sales page 1/1"; lead picks P7', R3, R10): asked from the portal while the
  // customer's ask-kinds switch lists it (PortalSettings.productionAskKinds, B-SA-046), answered by Sales.
  /// A change to the design of some of the order's lines: their words (required), the lines (one row each, no size, the
  /// pieces unchanged) and up to 10 of the order's files. Accepted only for a style of the customer's own private label: the
  /// office raises a product change request per style (changes.prisma ChangeRequest.orderChangeRequestId).
  DESIGN
}

/// OPEN → ACCEPTED | REFUSED (the office) | WITHDRAWN (the customer).
enum OrderChangeRequestStatus {
  OPEN
  ACCEPTED
  REFUSED
  WITHDRAWN
  /// B-PR-23: the office countered (a date, a fee, words) and waits for the customer's answer to its COUNTER_OFFER approval
  /// request: → ACCEPTED (the customer said yes; the office records it) | REFUSED (the office) | WITHDRAWN.
  COUNTERED
}

/// One cell a change or cancel request asks for: an order line, one of its sizes (or the line as a whole: a
/// made-to-measure unit, a line cancelled whole), the pieces it held when they asked and the pieces they ask for (0
/// removes them; a cancel asks 0). Written with the request, while it is OPEN; never changed or removed. A CANCEL with no
/// rows asks for the whole order. B-PR-23: a change may also ask a line in another colourway; a SPLIT_SHIPMENT's rows are
/// its first part (1 to the pieces before); a SAMPLE_ROUND names at most one line; a RUSH, HOLD or RESUME asks for the
/// whole order (no rows). B-SA-005: a DESIGN request names at least one line, each once, as a whole (no size), the pieces
/// unchanged (asked = before).
model OrderChangeRequestLine {
  id             String   @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId       String   @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The request's party (the partner role's policy key).
  partyId        String   @db.Uuid
  requestId      String   @db.Uuid
  /// A line of the request's order.
  orderLineId    String   @db.Uuid
  /// A size code of the line; null: the line as a whole.
  size           String?
  /// The pieces as they were when asked (what the customer saw), and the pieces asked; both at least 0.
  quantityBefore Int
  quantity       Int
  /// B-PR-23: a change's new colourway for the line (another colourway of the order line's style), with that style as the
  /// colourway's reference key; both or neither, a change only.
  styleId        String?  @db.Uuid
  colourwayId    String?  @db.Uuid
  createdAt      DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// The partner user who asked.
  createdById    String?  @db.Uuid

  request   OrderChangeRequest @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId, requestId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  orderLine SalesOrderLine     @relation("OrderChangeRequestLineOrderLine", fields: [tenantId, partyId, orderLineId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // B-PR-23. Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId.
  colourway Colourway?         @relation("OrderChangeRequestLineColourway", fields: [tenantId, styleId, colourwayId], references: [tenantId, styleId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([tenantId, requestId, orderLineId, size])
}

/// One card or SEPA payment of a deposit request or an invoice at the payment provider (FIN-118, FIN-123; design links.pay
/// "Pay by card", portal.customer.orders "Pay the deposit"): what it pays, how much, at which provider account and under
/// which of the provider's ids, and how it ended. The provider's own fields take the card or the mandate: no card number,
/// expiry, security code or client secret ever reaches our database. Made by the API (in the tenant's system context)
/// before it calls the provider; moved by the provider's signed webhook (a repeated webhook changes nothing); when it
/// succeeded, the payments command records its Payment (allocated to the deposit request or the invoice) and names it
/// here. CREATED → WAITING (the bank asks: 3-D Secure, a SEPA debit clearing) → SUCCEEDED | FAILED | CANCELLED; CREATED →
/// SUCCEEDED | FAILED | CANCELLED too. The last three are final. A retry is a new intent. Never deleted. Live card
/// payments wait for the Owner's yes with the provider's exact cost (GATE-SPEND); the FAKE provider until then.
model PaymentIntent {
  id                String              @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId          String              @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The company paid, and the party paying (the partner role's policy key).
  companyId         String              @db.Uuid
  partyId           String              @db.Uuid
  /// What it pays, exactly one (of the same company and party): an OPEN deposit request, or an issued TD01 / TD24
  /// invoice (a TD02 is paid through its deposit request; a credit note is not paid).
  depositRequestId  String?             @db.Uuid
  invoiceId         String?             @db.Uuid
  method            PaymentIntentMethod
  /// The amount asked of the provider, in minor units of the currency; above 0 and at most what it pays (the deposit
  /// request's amount, the invoice's gross total).
  /// @grain price
  amount            Int
  /// ISO 4217: the currency of what it pays.
  currency          String
  /// The payment provider's account (integration.prisma IntegrationAccount of provider PAYMENT_FAKE or STRIPE), of the
  /// company or tenant-wide.
  providerAccountId String              @db.Uuid
  /// The provider's own id of the intent (Stripe's `pi_…`), once it answered; unique per account, set once. Letters,
  /// digits, `_` and `-` only, never a run of twelve digits or more (no card number can be kept here).
  providerRef       String?
  status            PaymentIntentStatus @default(CREATED)
  /// FAILED: the provider's reason code ("card_declined"), told in our words; the same letters as providerRef.
  failureCode       String?
  /// When it reached SUCCEEDED, FAILED or CANCELLED; set exactly then.
  finishedAt        DateTime?           @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// SUCCEEDED: the Payment the payments command recorded for it (of the same company and party, the same amount and
  /// currency); set once.
  paymentId         String?             @db.Uuid
  /// The link it was started from (a PAYMENT or DEPOSIT_INFO link of the same company and party); null: from the portal
  /// (createdById names the partner user).
  linkId            String?             @db.Uuid
  version           Int                 @default(1)
  createdAt         DateTime            @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt         DateTime            @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// The partner user who started it in the portal (null by link, or the system).
  createdById       String?             @db.Uuid

  company         Company            @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  party           Party              @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  // Restrict, not Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId, companyId and partyId.
  depositRequest  DepositRequest?    @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, depositRequestId], references: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  invoice         Invoice?           @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, invoiceId], references: [tenantId, companyId, buyerPartyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  providerAccount IntegrationAccount @relation(fields: [tenantId, providerAccountId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  payment         Payment?           @relation(fields: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, paymentId], references: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  link            OneOffLink?        @relation(fields: [tenantId, partyId, linkId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  // The provider's id is unique per account (its webhook names it); a payment is made by one intent.
  @@unique([tenantId, providerAccountId, providerRef])
  @@unique([tenantId, paymentId])
  @@index([tenantId, depositRequestId])
  @@index([tenantId, invoiceId])
  @@index([tenantId, status])
}

/// How the customer pays at the provider (design links.pay "Method: Card · SEPA Direct Debit"). A bank transfer has no
/// intent (W1's DEPOSIT_INFO way, always shown).
enum PaymentIntentMethod {
  CARD
  SEPA_DEBIT
}

/// CREATED (made, the provider called) → WAITING (the bank asks: 3-D Secure, a SEPA debit clearing) → SUCCEEDED | FAILED |
/// CANCELLED; the last three are final.
enum PaymentIntentStatus {
  CREATED
  WAITING
  SUCCEEDED
  FAILED
  CANCELLED
}

/// "I paid" (owb-b1, schema wave "order workflow 1/1"; PL-schema § 5A row 4): the customer's buyer tells us it paid for one of
/// its orders (the whole order, a deposit request or a step of its payment plan), how much, on which day, how, with a note
/// and a proof (a file). It is a notice, not a payment: the office records the payment itself with its own command and
/// then marks the notice RECORDED, or DISMISSED (it found no such payment). A portal session inserts it OPEN for its own
/// party (portal.payments.notify); the office answers it once (OPEN → RECORDED | DISMISSED, with when and by whom); nothing
/// else changes and nothing is deleted (the …_order_workflow_guards trigger, G7). The customer reads its own notices,
/// never who in the office answered.
model PaymentNotice {
  id               String             @id @db.Uuid
  tenantId         String             @default(dbgenerated("(NULLIF(current_setting('factory.tenant_id'::text, true), ''::text))::uuid")) @db.Uuid
  /// The order's company and customer (the foreign key; the partner role's policy key).
  companyId        String             @db.Uuid
  partyId          String             @db.Uuid
  salesOrderId     String             @db.Uuid
  /// What it pays, when the customer said: a deposit request of the order, or a step of its payment plan (null: the order).
  depositRequestId String?            @db.Uuid
  milestoneId      String?            @db.Uuid
  /// How much the customer says it paid, in minor units of `currency` (above 0: the API).
  /// @grain price
  amount           Int
  /// ISO 4217.
  currency         String
  /// The day the customer says it paid (not in the future: the API).
  paidOn           DateTime           @db.Date
  /// How, in the customer's words ("Bank transfer"); null: not said.
  method           String?
  /// The customer's note to us; null: none.
  note             String?
  /// The proof (a bank receipt): a file of the order shared with its customer; null: none.
  fileId           String?            @db.Uuid
  state            PaymentNoticeState @default(OPEN)
  /// The office's answer: when and by whom, set exactly with RECORDED or DISMISSED, once. Who is hidden from the partner role.
  answeredAt       DateTime?          @db.Timestamptz(3)
  answeredById     String?            @db.Uuid
  version          Int                @default(1)
  createdAt        DateTime           @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt        DateTime           @default(now()) @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// The customer's person who told us (or the office person who typed it for the customer).
  createdById      String?            @db.Uuid

  // The order of the same company and customer; the deposit request and the step of that customer (Restrict, not
  // Prisma's SetNull default for an optional relation: that would also clear tenantId, companyId and partyId).
  salesOrder     SalesOrder           @relation("PaymentNoticeOrder", fields: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, salesOrderId], references: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  depositRequest DepositRequest?      @relation("PaymentNoticeDeposit", fields: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, depositRequestId], references: [tenantId, companyId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  milestone      SalesOrderMilestone? @relation("PaymentNoticeMilestone", fields: [tenantId, partyId, milestoneId], references: [tenantId, partyId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  file           StoredFile?          @relation("PaymentNoticeFile", fields: [tenantId, fileId], references: [tenantId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  // An order's notices (the Money tab), the open ones first.
  @@index([tenantId, salesOrderId, state])
  // The office's open notices of a customer.
  @@index([tenantId, partyId, state])
}

/// Where an "I paid" notice stands (owb-b1): OPEN → RECORDED (the office recorded the payment) | DISMISSED (no such payment
/// found). The last two are final.
enum PaymentNoticeState {
  OPEN
  RECORDED
  DISMISSED
}
